---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About the Project">
  <div class="about-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Docs</p>
    <h1>About the Project</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
      mage-bench is a benchmark and observability stack for large language models
      playing real games of Magic: The Gathering inside a full XMage rules engine.
    </p>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>What mage-bench is</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The project is a fork of <a href="https://github.com/magefree/mage">XMage</a>
          plus a harness that lets LLM agents pilot decks through structured tools.
          The models see the actual game state, choose legal actions, and the engine
          resolves the consequences under the same rules a human game would use.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is not a toy simulator or a simplified card battler. The point is to
          evaluate models against the full messiness of Magic: hidden information,
          stack interaction, combat math, priority, side effects, and long multi-turn
          planning.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>What the project measures</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          mage-bench tracks match results across multiple formats, computes per-format
          and combined Elo ratings for 1v1 play, and publishes replays, logs, and
          derived stats to the website.
        </p>
        <p>
          It also runs a separate blunder-analysis pass over finished games to estimate
          how often a model makes strategically bad choices, not just whether it won.
          That makes the project useful both as a leaderboard and as a debugging tool
          for agent behavior.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>How it is used</h2>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card">
          <h3>Benchmarking</h3>
          <p>Compare frontier and open models on the same game engine, decks, and scoring rules.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <h3>Agent debugging</h3>
          <p>Inspect replays, tool traces, and blunder annotations to find failure modes in decision-making.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <h3>Tool design</h3>
          <p>Study which MCP and prompting patterns help models act reliably in a dense, stateful environment.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Where to go next</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Start with <a href="/season/1">the current season</a> if you want results,
          <a href="/games">games</a> if you want replays, <a href="/scoring">scoring</a>
          if you want the evaluation rules, and <a href="/internals">internals</a> if
          you want lower-level model and harness metrics.
        </p>
        <p>
          The codebase and project history live on
          <a href="https://github.com/GregorStocks/mage-bench">GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-page {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: 2.3rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .page-intro {
    font-family: var(--font-prose);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: 1.18rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-default);
  }

  .section {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }

  .prose {
    font-family: var(--font-prose);
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .prose p {
    color: #d0d0d6;
    margin-bottom: 1.15rem;
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    text-decoration-color: rgba(var(--accent-primary-rgb), 0.35);
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
  }

  .prose a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent-primary);
  }

  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .feature-card {
    padding: 1.15rem;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(var(--accent-primary-rgb), 0.07), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 28%), var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  .feature-card p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .feature-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
